  while ((t - atomic_load_explicit(&rhead, memory_order_acquire)) == RING_SIZE) ; // spin
  ring[t & (RING_SIZE-1)] = b;
  atomic_store_explicit(&rtail, t+1, memory_order_release);
}
```
Wait, standard SPSC: producer owns rtail (only producer stores), reads rhead (acquire). Consumer owns rhead, reads rtail (acquire). Producer stores rtail with release. Yes as written — but producer must re-read t? t only changes by producer itself, so load once then spin re-checking rhead only. That's the correct pattern:

```c
static void ring_push(block_t* b) {
  size_t t = atomic_load_explicit(&rtail, memory_order_relaxed);
  while (t - atomic_load_explicit(&rhead, memory_order_acquire) == RING_SIZE) continue;
